<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis II, Duke of Bourbon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1337–1410</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Louis the Good</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis II, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, called the Good Duke, was a French prince who fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a> and led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> in 1390. His marriage to Anne, heiress of Forez, and his inheritance of Beaujolais greatly enlarged the Bourbon lands, which became one of the largest princely territories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-ii-duke-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="Louis II, Duke of Bourbon" width="320" height="704" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_II_de_Bourbon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
